From c6faee9ae0c641cee806bc5cd15a02188018845c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Galih Tama <galpt@v.recipes>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 01:30:16 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 23/23] v4.8-gpu: count EMA climbs in the 7.2 port

The 7.2 v4.7 port never incremented infinity_ema_climb_count, so the
'EMA climbs' row in infinity_stats read zero on the 7.2 arch.  Add the
increment at the climb site, matching the 7.1 reference, so the
monitoring surface reports the same signal on every arch.

Signed-off-by: Galih Tama <galpt@v.recipes>
---
 kernel/sched/infinity_sched.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/kernel/sched/infinity_sched.c b/kernel/sched/infinity_sched.c
index 697a4006c..a505fe83c 100644
--- a/kernel/sched/infinity_sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/infinity_sched.c
@@ -487,6 +487,7 @@ void infinity_consume(struct infinity_ctx *ctx, u64 delta_ns,
 	if (step > INFINITY_BUDGET_MAX_NS - ctx->ema)
 		step = INFINITY_BUDGET_MAX_NS - ctx->ema;
 	ctx->ema += step;
+	atomic64_inc(this_cpu_ptr(&infinity_ema_climb_count));
 }
 /* ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
 /* infinity_wakeup -- EMA decay on wakeup                               */
